# studies-archive-adam-optimizer

> **The retired 5-stage Adam reconstruction pipeline**: its 3-D event and optimisation-path Plotly
> displays, the cone↔surface intersection helpers they need, and the composite losses it minimised
> (`WC_loss` — whose first parameter `sensor_points` is never read in its body — and
> `compute_simplified_loss`'s centroid/intensity/spread terms). Superseded by the damped Gauss-Newton
> stack in `lucid.fitting` and by the Poisson + first-arrival losses.
>
> The displays read `optimization_results['history']['combined_losses'|'parameters'|'vertex_losses']`,
> a schema the library no longer produces, so they will not run against post-`eaf2e89f` output.
>
> Also here: the `tau_vtx = a·N_rays + b·E + c` hyperparameter fit used by the Adam-era vertex loss.
> Its scan driver (`s3df_jobs/submit_tau_hyperparameter_tuning_job.py`) was deleted from the tree;
> recover it with `git log --diff-filter=D -- s3df_jobs/`. Regenerate all three constants together or
> not at all.

